    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0427" n="[403]" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg403"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Thayer.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 14, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch of the 1st ultimo, No. 45,
                    communicating intelligence of the death of Mr. Charles March, late United States
                    vice-consul at Cairo, was duly received and has been made public here, where the
                    deceased was well and favorably known. The circumstances which attended his
                    sudden and unexpected death, with your just and feeling tribute to his character
                    and attainments, will possess a melancholy interest to his friends and to the
                    public generally.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William S. Thayer</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Alexandria.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
